-- ---- the definitions that paragraphs 55, 66, 75 and 76 carry ----

-- src:20616 | 55 A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting a recognised investment exchange , a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD to exercise its functions as such.“ Recognised investment exchange ” , “recognised clearing house” and “recognised CSD” have the same meaning as in section 285 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000.
@ref sch 11A para 55 "recognised investment exchange", "recognised clearing house" and "recognised CSD" have the same meaning as in section 285 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (src:20616-20616)
GIVEN `section 285 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000: the body is a recognised investment exchange, a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11A para 55 the body is a recognised investment exchange, a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD` MEANS
    `section 285 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000: the body is a recognised investment exchange, a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when that Act is not among the sources

-- src:20627 | 66 A disclosure for the purpose of enabling or assisting an overseas regulatory authority to exercise its regulatory functions.“ Overseas regulatory authority ” and “ regulatory functions ” have the same meaning as in section 82 of the Companies Act 1989.
@ref sch 11A para 66 "overseas regulatory authority" and "regulatory functions" have the same meaning as in section 82 of the Companies Act 1989 (src:20627-20627)
GIVEN `section 82 of the Companies Act 1989: the body is an overseas regulatory authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11A para 66 the body is an overseas regulatory authority` MEANS
    `section 82 of the Companies Act 1989: the body is an overseas regulatory authority` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when that Act is not among the sources

-- src:20640 | 75 A disclosure with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, disciplinary proceedings relating to the performance by a relevant lawyer, foreign lawyer, auditor, accountant, valuer or actuary of his professional duties. In this paragraph—
-- src:20641 | “ foreign lawyer ” means a person (other than a relevant lawyer) who is a foreign lawyer within the meaning of section 89(9) of the Courts and Legal Services Act 1990;
-- src:20642 | “ relevant lawyer ” means—
-- src:20643 | (a) a person who, for the purposes of the Legal Services Act 2007, is an authorised person in relation to an activity which constitutes a reserved legal activity (within the meaning of that Act),
-- src:20644 | (b) a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland, or
-- src:20645 | (c) a solicitor or advocate in Scotland.
@ref sch 11A para 75 "relevant lawyer" (src:20640-20645)
GIVEN `the person is, for the purposes of the Legal Services Act 2007, an authorised person in relation to an activity which constitutes a reserved legal activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a solicitor or advocate in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11A para 75 the person is a relevant lawyer` MEANS
    IF    `the person is, for the purposes of the Legal Services Act 2007, an authorised person in relation to an activity which constitutes a reserved legal activity`
       OR `the person is a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland`
       OR `the person is a solicitor or advocate in Scotland`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“ relevant lawyer ” means—"

-- src:20646 | 76 A disclosure with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, disciplinary proceedings relating to the performance by a public servant of his duties.“ Public servant ” means an officer or employee of the Crown.
@ref sch 11A para 76 "public servant" (src:20646-20646)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or employee of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11A para 76 the person is a public servant` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer or employee of the Crown`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“ Public servant ” means an officer or employee of the Crown"

§§ `Part 3 -- Overseas regulatory bodies`

-- src:20650 | 79 A disclosure is made in accordance with this Part of this Schedule if it is made to an approved third country competent authority in accordance with section 1253B (requests from approved third country competent authorities).
@ref sch 11A para 79 A disclosure to an approved third country competent authority in accordance with section 1253B (src:20650-20650)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made to an approved third country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1253B Requests from approved third country competent authorities` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11A para 79 the disclosure is made in accordance with this Part of this Schedule` MEANS
    IF NOT `the disclosure is made to an approved third country competent authority`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A disclosure is made in accordance with this Part of this Schedule if it is made to an approved third country competent authority"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1253B Requests from approved third country competent authorities`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in accordance with section 1253B"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1253B (coa27)

-- src:20651 | 80 A disclosure is made in accordance with this Part of this Schedule if it is—
-- src:20652 | (a) a transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority in accordance with rules imposed under paragraph 16A of Schedule 10 (transfer of papers to third countries), or
-- src:20653 | (b) a disclosure other than a transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports made to a third country competent authority for the purpose of enabling or assisting the authority to exercise its functions.
@ref sch 11A para 80 A transfer of papers under paragraph 16A of Schedule 10, or another disclosure to a third country competent authority (src:20651-20653)
GIVEN `the disclosure is a transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is in accordance with rules imposed under paragraph 16A of Schedule 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made to a third country competent authority for the purpose of enabling or assisting the authority to exercise its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11A para 80 the disclosure is made in accordance with this Part of this Schedule` MEANS
    IF    (`the disclosure is a transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority` AND `the transfer is in accordance with rules imposed under paragraph 16A of Schedule 10`)
       OR ((NOT `the disclosure is a transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority`) AND `the disclosure is made to a third country competent authority for the purpose of enabling or assisting the authority to exercise its functions`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A disclosure is made in accordance with this Part of this Schedule if it is"
